# ── Cloudflare R2 (private session recordings) ──────────────────────────────
# Create a free Cloudflare account → R2 → create a bucket (e.g. "bridgeway-recordings").
# Then R2 → "Manage API Tokens" → create an Account API token (Object Read & Write)
# scoped to the bucket. That gives the Access Key ID + Secret. Account ID is on the
# R2 overview page. Finally, add a CORS rule on the bucket so the admin upload works:
#   [{ "AllowedOrigins": ["http://localhost:3000","https://YOUR-DOMAIN"],
#      "AllowedMethods": ["PUT","GET"], "AllowedHeaders": ["*"] }]
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=
